    {
      "id": "93b2073cf619-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "Q. How many girls are taller than Samir in his class? (I) When students of Samir’s class are ranked in descending order of their height, Samir’s rank is 17th from the top among all the students and 12th among boys. (II) Samir’s rank from the bottom on the basis of height among boys is 18th and among all students is 29th",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Q. How many girls are taller than Samir in his class?</p><p>(I) When students of Samir’s class are ranked in descending order of their height, Samir’s rank is 17th from the top among all the students and 12th among boys.</p><p>(II) Samir’s rank from the bottom on the basis of height among boys is 18th and among all students is 29th</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>From I: (17 – 12) = 5 girl students are taller than Samir</p><p>From II: (29 – 18) = 11 girl students are shorter than Samir. But, from II alone it is not known how many girls are there in the class.</p><p>Hence, Data in statement I alone is sufficient to answer the question while data in statement II is not.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
