      "id": "93b2073cf619-q27",
      "number": 27,
      "question": "Statement: A large private bank has decided to retrench one-third of its employees in view of the huge losses incurred by it during the past three quarters. Course of action: I. The Government should issue a notification to general public to immediately stop all transactions with the bank. II. The Government should direct the bank to refrain from retrenching its employees. III. The Government should ask the central bank of the country to initiate an enquiry into the bank’s activities and submit its report.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Statement: A large private bank has decided to retrench one-third of its employees in view of the huge losses incurred by it during the past three quarters.</p><p>Course of action: </p><p>I. The Government should issue a notification to general public to immediately stop all transactions with the bank.</p><p>II. The Government should direct the bank to refrain from retrenching its employees.</p><p>III. The Government should ask the central bank of the country to initiate an enquiry into the bank’s activities and submit its report.</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>I. The Government should issue a notification to the general public to immediately stop all transactions with the bank. This course of action is not a logical response to the situation. Stopping all transactions with the bank would likely worsen the bank's financial situation and potentially lead to more significant issues, affecting not only the bank but also its customers and the overall economy. Therefore, this action does not follow logically.</p><p>II. The Government should direct the bank to refrain from retrenching its employees. This course of action suggests that the government should intervene and prevent the bank from retrenching its employees. While protecting jobs is a noble goal, it's essential to consider that the bank is facing financial losses. If the bank cannot sustain its current workforce due to its financial situation, preventing layoffs might not be a practical solution and could lead to further financial instability for the bank. Therefore, this action may not be a logical or feasible response.</p><p>III. The Government should ask the central bank of the country to initiate an inquiry into the bank’s activities and submit its report. This course of action is a reasonable response to the situation. When a large private bank faces financial difficulties and significant losses, it is essential to investigate the bank's activities to understand the root causes of these losses. An inquiry by the central bank can help identify any irregularities, mismanagement, or other factors contributing to the bank's financial troubles. Based on the findings of the inquiry, appropriate measures can be taken to address the situation and prevent similar issues in the future. Therefore, this action follows logically.</p><p>So, the correct answer is (c) Only III follows.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
